{"id":9195,"date":"2025-07-04T18:19:24","date_gmt":"2025-07-04T18:19:24","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/?p=9195"},"modified":"2025-07-15T16:22:38","modified_gmt":"2025-07-15T16:22:38","slug":"do-i-need-rodent-control-after-renovation-the-truth-you-must-know","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/do-i-need-rodent-control-after-renovation-the-truth-you-must-know\/","title":{"rendered":"Do I Need Rodent Control After Renovation? The Truth You Must Know"},"content":{"rendered":"<h2><b>You just renovated your dream home\u2014but something\u2019s scratching in the walls?<\/b><\/h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">That fresh paint smell, new flooring, and improved space feel great. But right after renovation, your home is also more vulnerable to a hidden problem many homeowners don\u2019t see coming: rodents.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While renovations bring aesthetic improvements, they can also create the perfect conditions for pests. Mice and rats are always looking for new shelter, warmth, and access to food\u2014and post-reno homes provide all of that and more.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wondering if you need cheap rodent control after a renovation? The short answer is yes\u2014and in this article, we\u2019ll explain why it\u2019s one of the smartest post-reno investments you can make.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Renovation Attracts Rodents<\/span><\/h2>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-7444\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/07\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-07-03-at-2.59.41-PM-300x200.jpeg\" alt=\"How Renovation Attracts Rodents \" width=\"300\" height=\"200\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may not notice it during the excitement of construction, but renovations often stir up more than dust. Rodents living nearby\u2014whether in walls, roofs, or garden sheds\u2014can be displaced during the process.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the same time, the work itself can unintentionally make your home more accessible to pests.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Here&#8217;s how:<\/b><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><b> Disturbed Nesting Sites<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Demolition or landscaping may force rodents out of their original hiding spots. With parts of your home open or exposed, they may simply move closer\u2014in some cases, right inside your walls or roof.<\/span><\/p>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><b> New Entry Points<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common during renovations, openings for plumbing, electrical wiring, or vent installation can leave small gaps behind. Even holes the size of a 20-cent coin are enough for a mouse to squeeze through.<\/span><\/p>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><b> Construction Debris and Food Scraps<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents are opportunistic. If your contractor or trades leave behind crumbs, food wrappers, or waste in bins or around the site, that\u2019s a buffet to them.<\/span><\/p>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li><b> Increased Warmth and Shelter<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fresh insulation, new wall cavities, or enclosed decks create comfortable, quiet spaces\u2014ideal for nesting. Once inside, rodents are quick to settle and even quicker to breed.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Renovating your home can be an exciting time, but if you&#8217;re not careful, it can also invite in unwanted guests that stay long after the work is finished.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hidden Rodent Entry Points Created During Renovation<\/span><\/h3>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-7445\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/07\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-07-03-at-3.04.20-PM-300x200.jpeg\" alt=\"Hidden Rodent Entry Points Created During Renovation \" width=\"300\" height=\"200\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents don\u2019t need a front door. They look for gaps, cracks, or vulnerabilities you may not even notice.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here are some of the most common rodent entry points introduced during renovation:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Foundation cracks<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Even hairline cracks in your foundation can provide entry from underneath your home.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Gaps in rooflines or under tiles<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Roof work often involves removing and replacing sections\u2014leaving tiny gaps where rodents can climb in.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Openings around new plumbing or electrical installations<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pipes and wires often go through walls and floors. If not sealed properly, these become rodent highways.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Crawlspaces, skirting boards, and wall cavities<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If left open during renovations, these provide easy access to interior spaces.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><b>Tip:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Take photos during the renovation process and label potential weak spots. You can use these later to help your pest control expert identify entry points faster.<\/span><\/p>\n<h4><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Real Dangers of Ignoring Rodent Control After Renovation<\/span><\/h4>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-7446\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/07\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-07-03-at-3.11.45-PM-300x158.jpeg\" alt=\"Real Dangers of Ignoring Rodent Control After Renovation \" width=\"300\" height=\"200\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents aren\u2019t just a nuisance. Left unchecked, they can pose serious health and safety risks:<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Chewed Wires = Fire Risk<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents love to gnaw\u2014and electrical wires are a prime target. This kind of damage isn&#8217;t just annoying; it can lead to short circuits and even house fires.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Contaminated Food Storage<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mice and rats often invade kitchens, pantries, and food containers. Their presence can result in contaminated food, and exposure to harmful bacteria such as salmonella.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Urine and Droppings = Health Hazards<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodent droppings and urine can trigger allergic reactions and spread diseases like leptospirosis and hantavirus.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Rapid Breeding<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A single pair of rodents can produce dozens of offspring in a short time. An unnoticed rodent family can turn into a full-blown infestation within weeks.<\/span><\/p>\n<h4><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Signs You Might Already Have a Rodent Problem<\/span><\/h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You might not see the rodents themselves, but they leave clues. Here\u2019s what to look (and listen) for:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Scratching or scurrying sounds<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in walls, ceilings, or under floors\u2014usually at night<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Rodent droppings<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, especially near food areas, bins, or behind appliances<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Gnaw marks<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on timber, wiring, or plastic fixtures<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Nesting material<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> like shredded insulation or paper in wall cavities or storage areas<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you spot one or more of these signs, it\u2019s likely time to take action.<\/span><\/p>\n<h5><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why Cheap Rodent Control Is the Smartest Post-Reno Investment<\/span><\/h5>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You\u2019ve spent good money improving your home\u2014so don\u2019t let rodents undermine it.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hiring a pest control service immediately after renovation may feel like an extra cost, but it actually saves you money and stress in the long run.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Here\u2019s why post-reno rodent control is a smart move:<\/b><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prevent serious damage before it starts<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Avoid expensive repairs from chewed wires, damaged insulation, or wall cavities<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Protect your health and that of your family<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Catch infestations early, while they\u2019re still manageable<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Get expert advice tailored to your new layout<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h6><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What a Professional Rodent Inspection Includes<\/span><\/h6>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A quality inspection looks beyond surface-level signs. Professional pest control teams know exactly where to look and what to look for.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here\u2019s what a comprehensive rodent inspection usually includes:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Checking for entry points<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in foundations, roofs, and utility lines<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Identifying nests<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> using heat and scent detection or visual inspection<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Assessing potential damage<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to insulation, wiring, and internal structures<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Applying safe, targeted removal<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> methods that won\u2019t harm pets or family<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Providing proofing advice<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to keep rodents from returning<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h5><b>Is Your Renovated Space Rodent-Safe?<\/b><\/h5>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Before settling into your new space, go through this quick post-renovation rodent-proofing checklist:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sealed all visible gaps in walls, floors, and ceilings<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Checked roof and attic access points<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Removed all leftover food and rubbish<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Inspected under sinks and around new appliances<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Scheduled a professional rodent inspection<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If anything is left unchecked, your home could be at risk. It\u2019s far easier to prevent a rodent problem than to get rid of one once it takes hold.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Renovation is an exciting step in homeownership. But while you&#8217;re focused on paint colours and tiles, rodents are looking for cracks and cavities. The dust may settle, but the risks can remain\u2014unless you take action.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">That\u2019s where <\/span><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> comes in. Based in Melbourne, 7 States Pest Control offers fast, affordable, and reliable pest management services tailored to your home\u2019s layout\u2014especially after renovation.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Their licensed technicians are experienced in identifying new pest entry points and providing cheap rodent control solutions that are safe, targeted, and effective.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Don\u2019t let mice or rats damage what you\u2019ve built. Even the most beautifully renovated homes in Melbourne can fall victim to pests if entry points are left unsealed or food sources are accessible.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The good news? Preventing an infestation doesn\u2019t have to be expensive. <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/rodent-control-melbourne\/\"><b>Cheap rodent control<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> services are available that offer thorough inspections, targeted treatment, and long-term protection\u2014without breaking the bank.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Protect your home investment\u2014<\/b><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/contact-us\/\"><b>book your rodent inspection now.<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> An affordable post-renovation pest check could be the smartest step you take after your build.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>You just renovated your dream home\u2014but something\u2019s scratching in the walls? That fresh paint smell, new flooring, and improved space feel great. But right after renovation, your home is also more vulnerable to a hidden problem many homeowners don\u2019t see coming: rodents. While renovations bring aesthetic improvements, they can also create the perfect conditions for [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":9199,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[21],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-9195","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-rodent-pest-control"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v25.4 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Rodent Control After Renovation | Cheap Rodent Control Melbourne<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Just renovated your home? Learn why rodents often move in after construction and why cheap rodent control is essential. Get a professional inspection in Melbourne today.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/do-i-need-rodent-control-after-renovation-the-truth-you-must-know\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Rodent Control After Renovation | Cheap Rodent Control Melbourne\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Just renovated your home? Learn why rodents often move in after construction and why cheap rodent control is essential. Get a professional inspection in Melbourne today.\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/do-i-need-rodent-control-after-renovation-the-truth-you-must-know\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta proper